Z||000000||dogtired||12-23-1999||07:16 AM||||OK I have read all the mine won't go up. Mine won't go down. Why is one up and the other down? (I hate relays)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">  Anyway.<BR>Started my car this morning, turned on the lights and got out to scrape ICE. I have noticed since I purchased the car that when in front of the garage door that the drivers side light isn't quite as bright as the other. (YES YES I know "not so bright")  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> I noticed that the drivers side bulb is not Halogen but the other is. That explains the difference but my question.<BR>What came as stock on the 86GT? Halogen or just normal bulbs?<BR>Does it make any difference? NO, but I would just like to know?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by dogtired (edited 12-23-1999).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||theogre||12-23-1999||09:29 PM||||few cars in the 80's using sealed beam lapms offered Halogen lighting.<P>If you want good lights try Phillips High Visibilty Halogen. (Part # H6054HV) They'll run you $25us or less for the pair.<P>The easy way tochange them is raise the lamps, unplug the motor, and shut off the lights. Then undo the bolt to the linkage at the bottom of the lamp frame. Change the lamp then put the linkage back on the frame.<P>The process is at least twice as fast that way and you only raise the hood once.||||reg||1
